      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because 50 mg is five times the maximum recommended daily dose of amlodipine. The usual adult range is 2.5\u201310 mg once daily, and 10 mg is the ceiling. A dose of 50 mg risks profound hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged vasodilatory shock. Normal kidney and liver function wouldn't change that.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **5 mg** by mouth once daily, the standard starting dose\n- **10 mg** by mouth once daily, the maximum dose\n- **2.5 mg** by mouth once daily, a lower starting dose sometimes used for frail patients or when adding to other antihypertensives\n\nTell me the dose you want and I'll enter it right away. If 50 mg is truly intended, for example because of a protocol I'm not aware of, please confirm that explicitly. I'd also suggest checking with pharmacy first."
      }
     ],
